From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: the writer packs several payloads into a packet, as Windows does (9111)

Every media object went into a 3200-byte packet of its own (one payload, the rest
padding), so a 128 kbps WMA file came out about four times the size Windows writes
(fre:ac, 5 s: 346 KB). Packets now carry as many payloads as fit (the ASF
specification's multiple payloads layout, WORD payload lengths, up to 63), objects
are split across packets as before, an object does not start in the last few bytes
of a packet, and the last packet goes out at EndWriting; the index counts the
packets a key frame spans, the one being filled included.
---
--- a/dlls/wmvcore/asfmux.c
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/asfmux.c
@@ -57,9 +57,14 @@
 static const GUID format_videoinfo = {0x05589f80, 0xc356, 0x11ce, {0xbf, 0x01, 0x00, 0xaa, 0x00, 0x55, 0x59, 0x5a}};
 
 #define PACKET_SIZE      3200
-#define PACKET_HEADER    13     /* error correction (3), length type and property flags, padding, send time, duration */
-#define PAYLOAD_HEADER   15     /* stream, object number, offset, replicated data length, replicated data (8) */
-#define PAYLOAD_SPACE    (PACKET_SIZE - PACKET_HEADER - PAYLOAD_HEADER)
+/* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9111): a packet carries as many payloads as fit, as Windows' writer packs
+ * them (each media object had a 3200-byte packet of its own: a 128 kbps WMA file came out four
+ * times the size). The multiple payloads layout of the ASF specification: */
+#define PACKET_HEADER    14     /* error correction (3), length type and property flags, padding, send time, duration, payload flags */
+#define PAYLOAD_HEADER   17     /* stream, object number, offset, replicated data length, replicated data (8), payload length */
+#define PAYLOAD_AREA     (PACKET_SIZE - PACKET_HEADER)
+#define MAX_PAYLOADS     63
+#define MIN_FRAGMENT     128    /* less room than this left for a split object: the packet goes out */
 #define INDEX_INTERVAL   10000000   /* one second */
 
